    "reason": "[ev-9fdf3ef2828b] is just a commit title. It doesn't define \"malformed\", name the tracking method or annotation, or say what triggers the wrong annotation, and nothing else in the section adds to it. The proposed undecidable leaf is justified as a runtime-behavior gap because manifests aren't in static inputs. That is the \"configuration might not be visible\" argument the rules exclude. The actual gap is in the evidence, and with no predicate expressible here, applicability should stay undetermined. Settling it needs the PR #22325 description or diff: what counts as a malformed resource, which tracking method is affected, and when the wrong annotation was written.",
